{
  "notes": [
    "Prototype portrait presets: presentation only, no game-rule effect. Not from Captain's Log.",
    "Each entry is Species + Gender + Variant -> image (head and shoulders) and fullBody (standing figure, used on Review). Images are ordinary files under public/; replace a file (or change its path) to swap the art. Missing files show the placeholder.",
    "Human (batch 01), Vulcan and Andorian head portraits are designer pixel art: transparent 256 x 320 PNGs used as both image and characterImage, so the backdrop shows behind them; the art wears command gold, recoloured through uniformMask (below). The other images are mock silhouettes. Mixed Heritage and New Species characters see every species' portraits for their gender (see rules/appearance.js).",
    "Composited head and shoulders (optional, components/useUniformImage.js): the character's chosen backdrop (portraitBackdrops.json, not part of the portrait), characterImage (the character on a transparent PNG) and uniformImage (optional greyscale overlay tinted with the department colour, see uniforms.json), drawn in that order into one picture. A portrait without characterImage shows image as before, with no backdrop (single images are opaque); one without image uses characterImage in its place. image stays the fallback if a layer file fails to load. characterImage and uniformImage must be the same pixel size; the backdrop is scaled to it.",
    "Optional uniformMask (the Human, Vulcan and Andorian portraits): a PNG the size of characterImage, opaque where the shirt is (scripts/makeUniformMask.mjs, checked by eye); uniformDivision is the division colour the art already wears (uniforms.json). The masked pixels are recoloured to the department colour, keeping their shading; the original PNG is never changed. Optional fullBodyLayers (fullBody): [{ role, src }] drawn bottom to top. Roles: background, uniform (tinted as above), face (face, hair, skin), insignia (optional; full body only for now). Mock layers: scripts/makePortraitLayers.mjs."
  ],
